WEBVTT

00:16.880 --> 00:20.920
I feel like I can do anything right now.

00:22.890 --> 00:26.510
I'm really really excited, Yuki-chan!

00:26.800 --> 00:29.500
Sumomo, there it is! The star drop!

00:30.350 --> 00:31.100
Yes!

00:32.420 --> 00:36.760
<i>It happened in the town closest to the stars.</i>

00:37.600 --> 00:40.800
<i>A very treasured story that only the two of them knew. </i>

00:41.410 --> 00:44.740
<i>Now, where should I begin first? </i>

01:03.160 --> 01:09.880
Shining stars away bless

01:03.700 --> 01:09.880
Shining stars away bless

01:10.210 --> 01:15.090
chiisakutonaeru mahou no kotobawa

01:10.210 --> 01:15.090
Silently chanting the magical words

01:15.970 --> 01:17.720
『onegai。。。』

01:15.970 --> 01:17.720
"please"

01:18.010 --> 01:23.350
hoshizora samayou kaze ni notta maigo notsubu

01:18.010 --> 01:23.350
The lost grain riding the wind on the sky

01:23.350 --> 01:24.390
『kizuite。。。』

01:23.350 --> 01:24.390
Please notice

01:24.390 --> 01:32.280
tsutawara nakute porori ochita kono omoi

01:24.390 --> 01:32.280
Untold words, teardrops of feelings that fell down

01:32.780 --> 01:39.370
kagayaki dasuyo GARASU bin nonaka

01:32.780 --> 01:39.370
Show your shine inside the glass bottle

01:39.740 --> 01:46.750
manten no hoshi deatta KISEKI kimi ga soba ni itekureru nara

01:39.740 --> 01:46.750
If you will stay beside me perfect star of encountered miracles...

01:46.910 --> 01:54.130
Whatever the mystery, I will be able to gather my courage.

01:47.330 --> 01:54.130
donna fushigi mouke tomeru yuuki umare te yuku yo

01:54.460 --> 02:01.720
nanatsuiro ni hikaru houseki sora kara mai oriru

01:54.460 --> 02:01.720
Seven colored glittering gems flying down from the sky

02:01.720 --> 02:05.430
Scoop up the important fragments

02:02.140 --> 02:05.430
daijina KAKERA sukui agerune

02:05.430 --> 02:10.940
kowasa nuyou sotto。。。

02:05.430 --> 02:10.940
And secretly hold onto them tight

02:22.310 --> 02:26.250
<i>The story started after school one day, in the month of May.</i>

02:27.440 --> 02:31.730
<i>I was taking my time thinking about the things I was told.</i>

02:31.730 --> 02:38.780
Hey Tsuwabuki, I know you're bad at socializing...

02:42.050 --> 02:46.120
Can't you try getting along better with everyone in class?

02:48.000 --> 02:49.490
<i>Even if you say that...</i>

02:50.010 --> 02:51.900
<i>What should I do?</i>

03:04.570 --> 03:06.000
Umm...

03:06.250 --> 03:09.980
<i>That was the start of everything. </i>

03:10.920 --> 03:15.000
What Color is Fate?

03:18.170 --> 03:22.840
<i>At that time, she had just transferred so I couldn't even remember her last name.</i>

03:25.810 --> 03:27.070
It's cold.

03:28.430 --> 03:29.950
Y-You're all wet.

03:30.650 --> 03:32.580
S-Sorry...

03:43.820 --> 03:44.480
Umm...

03:45.130 --> 03:48.220
What happened, Sumomo? Are you crying?

03:54.390 --> 03:57.940
I will never forgive someone who makes Sumomo cry!

03:59.280 --> 04:00.620
Nako-chan, wait!

04:04.870 --> 04:06.490
Well, well...

04:07.320 --> 04:10.670
Oh my, what an interesting combination.

04:11.210 --> 04:16.660
Akihime-san is close to tears, Yaeno-san is angry and Tsuwabuki-kun is here too.

04:16.990 --> 04:20.110
That's because he made Sumomo cry.

04:21.010 --> 04:22.680
That's not it, Nako-chan.

04:23.120 --> 04:25.120
Tsuwabuki-kun didn't do anything wrong.

04:27.390 --> 04:29.890
S-Sorry. I'm sorry!

04:30.410 --> 04:31.460
Sumomo?

04:31.460 --> 04:33.480
It's fine.

04:33.480 --> 04:35.430
It's alright, so...

04:35.720 --> 04:36.640
Hmm... I see!

04:37.910 --> 04:40.410
Well then, perfect timing.

04:40.410 --> 04:42.700
Perfect timing?

04:51.700 --> 04:55.700
Anyway, one of the basics of gardening is pulling out the weeds.

04:56.470 --> 04:59.850
This way, the sweet smelling May flowers are taken care of...

05:00.590 --> 05:03.030
Doing this gives you a nice feeling, doesn't it?

05:04.120 --> 05:06.290
Not that!

05:06.980 --> 05:10.150
Kisaragi-sensei, why did it come to this?

05:10.150 --> 05:15.150
Well, the Gardening Club only has two members. Akihime-san and Yaeno-san.

05:15.150 --> 05:19.060
That's right. Yaeno-san, can you hand that thing to Tsuwabuki-kun?

05:19.060 --> 05:19.830
Yes.

05:19.830 --> 05:20.970
Hey...

05:20.970 --> 05:24.960
You just came at the right time when we needed more people.

05:24.960 --> 05:25.990
Don't tell me...

05:26.770 --> 05:30.630
You are going to use this to lure me over to the Gardening Club?

05:30.630 --> 05:34.360
Just as expected, Tsuwabuki-kun. Good decision.

05:34.360 --> 05:38.500
Well then, I'll leave everything to you, the only male member.

05:38.560 --> 05:39.840
See ya.

05:39.860 --> 05:40.940
See ya... what?

05:40.940 --> 05:42.530
Tsuwabuki, here.

05:43.650 --> 05:46.240
Economical Sprinkler

05:43.650 --> 05:46.320
E
A
S
Y

05:43.650 --> 05:46.610
CONVENIENT

05:44.010 --> 05:46.100
The sprinkler framework.

05:52.250 --> 05:58.560
Tsuwabuki-kun, we've been in the new class for more than a month now...

05:59.000 --> 06:03.470
Excluding us, you've never talked to anyone else before, right?

06:04.270 --> 06:06.710
Everyone is worried, you know.

06:06.710 --> 06:09.140
Are you even listening, Tsuwabuki?

06:12.800 --> 06:14.960
About just now, Nako-chan...

06:14.960 --> 06:18.120
I dropped the watering pot when I bumped into him.

06:18.120 --> 06:23.670
Then I got surprised at Tsuwabuki-kun getting wet. And then, and then...

06:24.160 --> 06:26.220
I understand, Sumomo.

06:26.220 --> 06:26.870
Really?

06:28.010 --> 06:30.680
Thank goodness, Nako-chan.

06:36.750 --> 06:40.970
Wah, it's finished. This is great, really great, right?

06:40.970 --> 06:41.580
Yeah.

06:41.580 --> 06:43.420
He really did it.

06:43.630 --> 06:45.640
So where is Tsuwabuki now?

06:49.090 --> 06:51.660
I guess being in the Gardening Club's pretty tough too.

06:52.050 --> 06:54.270
It would be hard for just two girls.

06:55.860 --> 06:58.920
Eh, so I'll be a Gardening Club member, just like that?

07:06.060 --> 07:07.150
H-Hey you!

07:07.150 --> 07:09.470
Step aside, please step aside!

07:15.510 --> 07:17.020
I'm really sorry.

07:17.650 --> 07:20.690
Are you hurt anywhere?

07:20.690 --> 07:22.010
I'm fine but...

07:22.940 --> 07:24.380
Are those ears?

07:24.790 --> 07:26.030
Uwah!

07:26.270 --> 07:31.210
Err... this is cosplay, yes just cosplay.

07:32.300 --> 07:34.700
Cos... what?

07:34.810 --> 07:37.000
Here, I believe this is yours.

07:37.420 --> 07:39.480
I'll return it to you.

07:41.070 --> 07:42.380
Now, please excuse me!

07:43.540 --> 07:46.070
What was that all about?

07:59.880 --> 08:03.230
Huh? What? Hey, what the...?!

08:09.360 --> 08:11.770
Wah, this is so cute.

08:11.770 --> 08:13.120
Why is it here?

08:14.490 --> 08:17.840
Did someone forget it here or was it thrown away?

08:18.360 --> 08:20.170
I feel bad for you.

08:20.170 --> 08:21.520
What, what is this?

08:21.320 --> 08:23.050
You don't have to worry, alright?

08:22.720 --> 08:24.110
Huh, Akihime?

08:24.110 --> 08:26.230
I'll bring you home.

08:26.230 --> 08:27.940
Eh? W-What?

08:27.940 --> 08:30.290
What a cute little doll.

08:32.210 --> 08:34.630
Sumomo, is Tsuwabuki here?

08:35.310 --> 08:37.350
No, I didn't see him anywhere.

08:38.290 --> 08:39.590
Wait for a moment, okay?

08:39.830 --> 08:43.030
I'm looking for a friend named Tsuwabuki-kun.

08:43.030 --> 08:44.490
I'll be back soon.

08:45.290 --> 08:47.570
No, I'm right here.

08:48.140 --> 08:50.900
Is this a dream? What the hell is happening?

08:53.570 --> 08:57.360
"What the hell is happening?" indeed.

08:57.990 --> 08:59.250
K-Kisaragi-sensei!

09:00.690 --> 09:05.000
To think that the one who would receive the fate of the stars is this mysterious.

09:09.930 --> 09:12.350
W-Wait a second!

09:12.350 --> 09:14.660
What are you going to do?

09:15.820 --> 09:18.480
You don't have to worry, Tsuwabuki-kun.

09:19.260 --> 09:21.930
That's easy for you to say...

09:27.030 --> 09:29.860
Here, it won't hurt so...

09:30.050 --> 09:31.240
Uwahh!

09:31.240 --> 09:36.490
W-W-Wait a second...!

09:38.210 --> 09:38.990
There you go.

09:38.990 --> 09:41.860
Now you should be able to talk and move normally.

09:42.780 --> 09:44.000
Ah!

09:44.000 --> 09:47.340
You're right. I can speak!

09:47.340 --> 09:48.600
I can move!

09:48.600 --> 09:50.950
So, Tsuwabuki-kun...

09:51.790 --> 09:54.510
You must have drank a juice that was dropped from somewhere, didn't you?

09:55.560 --> 09:58.760
Huh? I wouldn't do such a thing...

09:58.760 --> 10:01.520
Wait... Just now, I bumped into a weird guy and then...

10:03.050 --> 10:03.810
That's it.

10:04.650 --> 10:07.780
That must be the reason why you transformed.

10:08.190 --> 10:11.820
That guy is someone from Figurare.

10:12.000 --> 10:13.380
Figu- what?

10:14.080 --> 10:19.230
Figu-ra-re. It is another world different than our world of Retroscena.

10:19.230 --> 10:23.400
And in that world, transformation is a normal phenomenon.

10:23.400 --> 10:24.760
Transformation.

10:24.760 --> 10:25.340
Right.

10:26.040 --> 10:30.560
Which means you drank the Figurare traveler's transformation potion.

10:30.560 --> 10:31.840
Do you understand...?

10:32.420 --> 10:34.000
Guess not.

10:34.410 --> 10:35.950
Of course not!

10:35.950 --> 10:38.250
There's no way I'd believe that Figura-whatever...

10:38.260 --> 10:39.600
Come in.

10:39.600 --> 10:40.810
Excuse me.

10:42.360 --> 10:46.010
Kisaragi-sensei, we couldn’t find Tsuwabuki-kun anywhere.

10:46.010 --> 10:50.470
Oh, he said he had some business to do so he went home earlier.

10:50.470 --> 10:51.810
I see.

10:52.380 --> 10:53.880
Looking for him about something?

10:54.430 --> 10:59.090
Yeah. He finished setting up the sprinkler so we wanted to say thanks.

10:59.090 --> 11:03.580
And there was a little misunderstanding earlier, so...

11:04.010 --> 11:07.630
Why don't you do that tomorrow then?

11:07.630 --> 11:10.130
It's getting dark now, so you both should head back too.

11:10.130 --> 11:11.350
Okay.

11:14.080 --> 11:19.610
Umm, did you see a doll? A cute little sheep.

11:19.610 --> 11:23.140
Hmm, I don't think so.

11:23.140 --> 11:25.150
I see. Goodbye.

11:30.140 --> 11:34.160
Well then, I'll tell you how to return to your old self.

11:34.160 --> 11:37.290
Huh? I can return to my old self? Really?

11:37.290 --> 11:38.190
Of course.

11:38.870 --> 11:43.200
However, a sheep like you wouldn't be able to do it.

11:43.670 --> 11:47.560
I wonder what kind of destiny is waiting for you.

12:14.200 --> 12:17.710
Today, I talked a lot with Tsuwabuki-kun.

12:32.630 --> 12:34.140
It's Doll-chan!

12:36.800 --> 12:40.550
Thank goodness, I thought I'd never see you again.

12:40.550 --> 12:42.650
What a strange doll.

12:42.980 --> 12:44.180
This is...?

12:45.210 --> 12:47.730
Why? Why did it have to be Akihime?

12:45.380 --> 12:47.330
It looks like a letter.

12:48.540 --> 12:50.110
Maybe it got stuck.

12:51.380 --> 12:55.110
Tsuwabuki-kun, I'm going to tell you how to return to your old self so...

12:56.330 --> 13:00.030
you can tell your soon-to-be-chosen girl partner about it.

13:00.870 --> 13:05.280
To begin with, this town is said to be the town nearest...

13:10.480 --> 13:12.020
Now, Tsuwabuki-kun.

13:12.020 --> 13:15.160
That ring will bring you to the chosen girl.

13:15.890 --> 13:17.260
Hey, wait!

13:17.260 --> 13:20.060
I will send you to your Stellar Spinear.

13:20.460 --> 13:21.590
Have a nice trip!

13:21.590 --> 13:24.740
Wait! Wait a second!

13:25.880 --> 13:29.310
Why? Why did the girl have to be Akihime?

13:29.310 --> 13:33.520
Hmm... "I'm a special doll."

13:33.520 --> 13:37.400
"Due to certain circumstances, I cannot go back to my home."

13:37.400 --> 13:39.780
"For me to return to the doll land,

13:39.780 --> 13:41.980
I will need your power."

13:41.980 --> 13:43.350
"If it's fine with you,

13:43.350 --> 13:46.030
please take care of and help save me."

13:46.600 --> 13:48.000
What's that supposed to mean?

13:49.160 --> 13:52.000
It talked, and it's moving too.

13:57.300 --> 14:01.800
Yay! This is great!

14:01.800 --> 14:04.500
It really is a special Doll-chan.

14:05.290 --> 14:09.060
I'm Akihime Sumomo. What is your name?

14:10.340 --> 14:11.060
Tsuwa-

14:11.440 --> 14:12.670
Tsuwabuki-kun.

14:12.670 --> 14:17.400
In order for you to change back, you mustn't tell anybody your real identity.

14:17.560 --> 14:19.130
If someone finds out...

14:20.300 --> 14:22.020
None, I have no name!

14:23.270 --> 14:24.770
Is that so?

14:24.770 --> 14:26.050
Yes.

14:27.260 --> 14:29.040
<i>That was really close.</i>

14:29.040 --> 14:31.820
<i>If my identity is known, I won't be able to return to my old self.</i>

14:33.770 --> 14:36.750
Umm, hey, what's the matter?

14:37.880 --> 14:39.700
I'm sorry.

14:39.700 --> 14:41.940
Not having a name...

14:41.940 --> 14:45.470
There must be a reason to it, right?

14:47.490 --> 14:53.020
I know! You're white, small and light, so... Yuki-chan.

14:54.030 --> 14:55.560
From now on, you'll be Yuki-chan.

14:56.720 --> 14:58.650
So I'm Yuki-chan, huh?

14:58.650 --> 15:05.810
Note:"Ore" is considered a more manly and commanding way of referring to one's self as opposed to "Boku".

14:58.650 --> 15:02.550
Hey, not 'Ore' but 'Boku' right?

15:02.550 --> 15:05.800
Just because you can't go home, you shouldn't act wild.

15:05.800 --> 15:06.570
Act wild?

15:07.660 --> 15:08.850
Yuki-chan.

15:08.850 --> 15:10.670
I'll do my best...

15:10.670 --> 15:13.190
So you can go back home.

15:13.190 --> 15:14.220
T-That's fine with you?

15:14.220 --> 15:17.480
Well, you need my help right?

15:17.480 --> 15:19.410
So what should I do?

15:20.660 --> 15:22.050
Well, for me to return...

15:22.280 --> 15:23.690
Use 'Boku'!

15:24.430 --> 15:26.580
For me to return...

15:27.690 --> 15:30.850
There are seven star drops.

15:30.850 --> 15:32.780
Star drops?

15:32.780 --> 15:37.330
The star drops can only be gathered by the chosen girl.

15:37.780 --> 15:39.820
And that's me?

15:41.010 --> 15:42.310
Looks like it.

15:42.730 --> 15:45.920
So, I'm the chosen girl.

15:46.220 --> 15:49.140
What would happen if I fail...?

15:49.140 --> 15:53.150
No, I must let Yuki-chan go back home.

15:53.150 --> 15:55.330
I'll do my best, Yuki-chan.

15:56.240 --> 15:57.560
Thank you.

15:58.080 --> 16:03.060
<i>Akihime... she looks so different compared to when she's at school...</i>

16:03.660 --> 16:06.340
Huh? That's right, the ring.

16:07.170 --> 16:09.020
A ring?

16:12.660 --> 16:15.620
Wow! This is great!

16:15.620 --> 16:19.700
When a star drop falls down, the ring will shine towards it.

16:20.000 --> 16:21.530
Guess it's real.

16:21.530 --> 16:23.290
Let's go, Yuki-chan.

16:30.310 --> 16:33.220
Hold on tight so you don't fall off, okay?

16:38.710 --> 16:39.670
Umm...

16:40.280 --> 16:41.710
Use the ring!

16:41.710 --> 16:42.990
Oh, right!

16:47.850 --> 16:50.220
So that is a star drop?

16:54.930 --> 16:57.180
It's going to drop near my school.

17:03.160 --> 17:06.420
I wonder where it dropped at, Yuki-chan.

17:06.420 --> 17:08.450
Umm...

17:08.450 --> 17:12.850
Oh yeah! The star drop likes to drop somewhere that has pretty water.

17:12.850 --> 17:14.080
Water?

17:21.700 --> 17:22.730
It should be here.

17:24.870 --> 17:26.900
But what's happening here?

17:26.900 --> 17:32.010
This fountain's supposed to be old and there shouldn't be water flowing out of it anymore.

17:33.270 --> 17:34.670
So that is the drop.

17:36.730 --> 17:38.850
But that looks deep.

17:39.280 --> 17:44.040
It isn't supposed to be this deep. I can't reach it.

17:57.460 --> 18:00.400
Yay, this is great!

18:00.510 --> 18:02.240
It's so great, so great!

18:02.240 --> 18:04.240
It's just like magic!

18:04.240 --> 18:10.040
If you don't hurry, the star drop will melt into the water!

18:11.220 --> 18:13.050
Oh no!

18:17.750 --> 18:20.380
I can't reach it at all, Yuki-chan.

18:20.380 --> 18:22.430
That's right, words!

18:22.660 --> 18:24.720
It's because we're not reading the detachment words.

18:30.700 --> 18:33.050
What... are these...

18:33.420 --> 18:34.690
...characters?

18:37.190 --> 18:39.370
This part shows the Japanese characters.

18:39.850 --> 18:41.890
Those blue characters are...

18:42.770 --> 18:43.460
That's... 'pu'!

18:43.920 --> 18:46.970
Next is 'ru'... 'vu'...

18:46.970 --> 18:49.480
And then...

18:50.400 --> 18:51.460
I think that's 'ra'.

18:51.460 --> 18:52.750
Eh?

18:52.750 --> 18:58.090
And then 'de', 'i', no... it's a small 'i'.

19:00.970 --> 19:04.880
Pu-ru-vu Ra-di!

19:09.110 --> 19:10.280
We have to catch up to it!

19:11.020 --> 19:12.440
Wait!

19:15.480 --> 19:16.950
Are you okay?

19:18.370 --> 19:22.830
I was worried that I'd step on the flowers, so I fell.

19:22.830 --> 19:23.880
I see.

19:24.460 --> 19:26.300
The star drop...

19:28.040 --> 19:29.520
Huh?

19:31.140 --> 19:32.230
Where did...?

19:43.010 --> 19:46.540
The star drop disappeared.

19:46.850 --> 19:49.090
I'm sorry, Yuki-chan.

19:49.090 --> 19:50.260
I'm not...

19:52.600 --> 19:58.380
Well, umm... it likes water so how about spraying some water?

19:58.380 --> 20:00.680
Use the sprinkler that we built today!

20:00.680 --> 20:01.520
Today?

20:03.120 --> 20:04.450
Whoops...

20:04.850 --> 20:07.540
I see, that sprinkler!

20:22.350 --> 20:23.470
There it is!

20:31.840 --> 20:34.260
Wow, it's pretty!

20:35.750 --> 20:38.210
Alright, this time I'll do it!

20:38.210 --> 20:40.980
But it didn't work too well even with the words, right?

20:40.980 --> 20:44.270
It must be because I was trying to get it from a difficult place.

20:44.270 --> 20:45.830
Let's go, Yuki-chan!

20:53.820 --> 20:55.810
Puruvu Radi!

21:04.870 --> 21:06.440
We did it.

21:06.600 --> 21:07.890
Yes.

21:08.960 --> 21:10.300
So pretty.

21:13.040 --> 21:15.260
Put it inside the glass flask we brought.

21:15.260 --> 21:16.480
Okay.

21:17.840 --> 21:19.140
Done.

21:22.790 --> 21:24.340
Yay!

21:24.340 --> 21:26.500
We did it, Yuki-chan!

21:30.390 --> 21:34.130
Miss, that girl must be her...

21:36.920 --> 21:40.780
Prima Palm, the one that will get in our way...

21:42.640 --> 21:45.660
I won't hand over the star drops.

21:51.410 --> 21:53.370
That was fun.

21:53.370 --> 21:56.400
That was my first time doing something so fun and mysterious.

21:56.530 --> 21:59.290
My heart was beating so fast.

21:59.770 --> 22:00.940
Beating so fast...

22:02.760 --> 22:08.920
But Yuki-chan, how did you know about the sprinkler that Tsuwabuki-kun built today...?

22:11.320 --> 22:14.580
That's because... umm... err...

22:16.550 --> 22:17.400
I...

22:27.950 --> 22:30.410
<i>The girl's name was Akihime Sumomo.</i>

22:31.780 --> 22:35.670
<i>And now, there are six star drops left.</i>

22:51.540 --> 22:55.090
kira kira no hoshikuzu ha maru de

22:51.540 --> 22:55.090
Fragments of glittering stars

22:55.090 --> 22:58.380
koi suru otome no kiseki

22:55.090 --> 22:58.380
are just like the miracles of a girl in love

22:58.630 --> 23:02.180
kinou mada no watashi ha doko he

22:58.630 --> 23:02.180
Where did the cleverness from yesterday go,

